  "implementation": [
    "Prepared metadata counts actual full frame-buffer capacities and dynamic frame children, all four JSON trees, optional range error and the full containing value once.",
    "Existing admission adds the actual Retained wrapper layout and one new Arc root before publishing Arc<Retained<Prepared>>. Shared immutable aliases keep this same guard through terminal queue, Ready, save worker and actual final drop.",
    "Working.previous retains the old Ready snapshot until known terminal reception. Input/target admission, parse and OS spawn failures preserve it; terminal cancellation/error/disconnection restores it. Save clones its shared input rather than consuming the only accepted snapshot before spawning.",
    "Thin QObject calls delegate existing preparation/poll/save bodies to a focused lifecycle module. Scientific preflight/encoding/publication remains in the same public Rust API; JSON keys, supported formats, limits and numerical results are preserved.",
    "One named terminal queue slot bounds transport cardinality. Deterministic launcher failure follows the existing shell worker test-seam pattern. No new public scientific API, accounting framework, schema, binding, Cargo dependency or CXX/QML registration.",
    "Saved Value/error envelopes and outer request/control/closure/channel infrastructure remain pending; this unit accepts Prepared products and Ready rollback only."
  ],
  "closes_earlier_coverage_gap": "session-designer-input-evidence.json: direct prior-Ready input rejection and both prepare/save spawn-failure runtime cases now pass through actual lifecycle handlers.",
